 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.14,
   "end": 2.02,
   "text": "Here's the thing most people get wrong."
  },
  {
   "start": 2.34,
   "end": 5.12,
   "text": "Rome didn't hire builders. Its soldiers were the builders."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.34,
   "end": 8.58,
   "text": "Men from three legions did most of the work: the Second Augusta,"
  },
  {
   "start": 8.86,
   "end": 9.9,
   "text": "the Sixth Victrix,"
  },
  {
   "start": 10.1,
   "end": 12.5,
   "text": "and the Twentieth Valeria Victrix."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.78,
   "end": 14.16,
   "text": "A legionary had to march,"
  },
  {
   "start": 14.44,
   "end": 14.6,
   "text": "fight,"
  },
  {
   "start": 14.8,
   "end": 18.22,
   "text": "dig, quarry, and lay stone. Each team built its own stretch. And when they finished,"
  },
  {
   "start": 18.4,
   "end": 22.78,
   "text": "they carved a stone with their unit's name on it, like signing a homework assignment."
  },
  {
   "start": 23.58,
   "end": 26.18,
   "text": "Archaeologists have found many of these building stones."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.4,
   "end": 29.86,
   "text": "Some are neat. Some look like they were carved on a Friday afternoon."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.06,
   "end": 33.44,
   "text": "The plan looked simple on paper. A stone wall, ten Roman feet thick,"
  },
  {
   "start": 33.62,
   "end": 35.98,
   "text": "and probably around fifteen feet tall. In front of it,"
  },
  {
   "start": 36.28,
   "end": 36.88,
   "text": "facing north,"
  },
  {
   "start": 37.16,
   "end": 37.7,
   "text": "a deep ditch."
  },
  {
   "start": 37.88,
   "end": 38.94,
   "text": "In the middle section,"
  },
  {
   "start": 39.16,
   "end": 42.58,
   "text": "the builders set the wall right on top of a line of cliffs called the Whin Sill,"
  },
  {
   "start": 42.8,
   "end": 43.9,
   "text": "so the ground did half the work."
  },
  {
   "start": 44.08,
   "end": 45.34,
   "text": "Every Roman mile,"
  },
  {
   "start": 45.72,
   "end": 48.44,
   "text": "a small fort called a milecastle,"
  },
  {
   "start": 48.72,
   "end": 50.72,
   "text": "with room for a small squad of soldiers."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.34,
   "end": 60.14,
   "text": "Between each pair of milecastles, two stone watchtowers called turrets. That's eighty milecastles and about a hundred and sixty turrets, lined up like beads on a string."
  },
  {
   "start": 60.36,
   "end": 65.38,
   "text": "And here's the detail that matters most. Every milecastle had two gates."
  },
  {
   "start": 65.64,
   "end": 67.4,
   "text": "One facing south. One facing north."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.68,
   "end": 68.6,
   "text": "Straight through the wall."
  },
  {
   "start": 68.92,
   "end": 70.26,
   "text": "Then the plan started changing."
  },
  {
   "start": 70.66,
   "end": 71.54,
   "text": "Partway through,"
  },
  {
   "start": 71.74,
   "end": 72.66,
   "text": "the wall got thinner."
  },
  {
   "start": 73.04,
   "end": 75.86,
   "text": "The builders cut it from ten feet down to about eight,"
  },
  {
   "start": 76.2,
   "end": 77.8,
   "text": "probably to save time and stone."
  },
  {
   "start": 78.12,
   "end": 80.24,
   "text": "In the west there was no good limestone for mortar,"
  },
  {
   "start": 80.76,
   "end": 83.12,
   "text": "so the western third of the wall was built from turf."
  },
  {
   "start": 83.78,
   "end": 88.42,
   "text": "Basically, a wall of stacked grass bricks. Then Rome decided milecastles weren't enough,"
  },
  {
   "start": 88.7,
   "end": 90.64,
   "text": "and moved big forts right onto the wall,"
  },
  {
   "start": 91.06,
   "end": 94.84,
   "text": "each holding hundreds of soldiers. And then came the strangest addition of all."
  },
  {
   "start": 95.4,
   "end": 96.04,
   "text": "Behind the wall,"
  },
  {
   "start": 96.28,
   "end": 97.0,
   "text": "on the Roman side,"
  },
  {
   "start": 97.2,
   "end": 100.8,
   "text": "they dug a second giant ditch between two earth banks. It's called the Vallum."
  },
  {
   "start": 101.3,
   "end": 102.12,
   "text": "It faced south."
  },
  {
   "start": 102.48,
   "end": 103.72,
   "text": "Toward their own province."
  },
  {
   "start": 103.96,
   "end": 105.94,
   "text": "Most of the wall went up in about six years."
  },
  {
   "start": 106.48,
   "end": 110.36,
   "text": "Day after day: quarry the stone, haul it, fill the middle with rubble and clay,"
  },
  {
   "start": 110.64,
   "end": 112.02,
   "text": "set the facing blocks, repeat."
  },
  {
   "start": 112.38,
   "end": 113.5,
   "text": "Seventy-three miles."
  },
  {
   "start": 113.78,
   "end": 117.04,
   "text": "And once it was finished, the legions marched back to their bases."
  },
  {
   "start": 117.24,
   "end": 120.12,
   "text": "The men who actually lived on the wall were auxiliaries,"
  },
  {
   "start": 120.34,
   "end": 123.5,
   "text": "soldiers recruited from conquered peoples across the empire."
  },
  {
   "start": 123.94,
   "end": 127.32,
   "text": "Tungrians and Batavians from what's now Belgium and the Netherlands."
  },
  {
   "start": 127.5,
   "end": 127.8,
   "text": "Later,"
  },
  {
   "start": 128.06,
   "end": 129.38,
   "text": "even archers from Syria."
  },
  {
   "start": 129.7,
   "end": 134.98,
   "text": "So the guard staring north into the British fog often wasn't British, and wasn't from Rome either."
  },
  {
   "start": 135.22,
   "end": 135.86,
   "text": "Just like you."
  },
  {
   "start": 136.16,
   "end": 137.6,
   "text": "And we know what their lives were like,"
  },
  {
   "start": 137.78,
   "end": 138.72,
   "text": "because they wrote things down."
  },
  {
   "start": 139.1,
   "end": 141.84,
   "text": "At Vindolanda, a fort just behind the wall line,"
  },
  {
   "start": 142.24,
   "end": 144.98,
   "text": "archaeologists found hundreds of thin wooden letters,"
  },
  {
   "start": 145.18,
   "end": 146.18,
   "text": "preserved in wet,"
  },
  {
   "start": 146.38,
   "end": 146.94,
   "text": "airless mud."
  },
  {
   "start": 147.4,
   "end": 154.12,
   "text": "One is a birthday party invitation from an officer's wife. One mentions a package of socks, sandals, and two pairs of underpants."
  },
  {
   "start": 154.32,
   "end": 156.82,
   "text": "One officer writes that his men have run out of beer,"
  },
  {
   "start": 157.04,
   "end": 158.28,
   "text": "and could someone please send more."
  },
  {
   "start": 158.6,
   "end": 161.34,
   "text": "One report sneers at the locals as 'Brittunculi.'"
  },
  {
   "start": 161.76,
   "end": 162.62,
   "text": "Little Brits."
  },
  {
   "start": 162.9,
   "end": 164.26,
   "text": "Life on the frontier was cold,"
  },
  {
   "start": 164.52,
   "end": 164.78,
   "text": "boring,"
  },
  {
   "start": 165.0,
   "end": 166.26,
   "text": "and full of paperwork."
  },
  {
   "start": 166.66,
   "end": 168.28,
   "text": "Which brings us back to that knock on the gate."
  },
  {
   "start": 168.56,
   "end": 171.56,
   "text": "If this wall had a door every mile... what was it actually for?"
  }
 ],
